 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "One word at the end changes everything",
     "texto": [
      "In Vietnamese, the tone of an order is given by the last word:",
      "**…đi** = come on, go on (encourages or hurries): «Ăn **đi**!» = Eat up, come on!",
      "**…nào** = let's, come on (invites doing it together or encourages): «Bắt đầu **nào**!» = Come on, let's begin!",
      "**…thôi** = right, just do it, and nothing more (it's time to): «Về **thôi**!» = Let's go now!",
      "**…đã** = first (before something else): «Rửa tay **đã**!» = Wash your hands first!",
      "**…nhé** = OK? (asks for agreement, softens): «Thái mỏng **nhé**» = Slice it thin, OK?",
      "They can be combined: «Ăn **đi nào**!», «Nghỉ một chút **đã nhé**»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Cooking verbs",
     "texto": [
      "**thái** (slice into strips or pieces), **băm** (mince), **trộn** (mix), **nêm** (season), **ướp** (marinate), **gói** / **cuốn** (wrap, roll), **rán** / **chiên** (fry: north / south), **luộc** (boil), **hấp** (steam), **xào** (stir-fry), **nướng** (grill), **nếm** (taste)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
